<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40901" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκύνιον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skin of the brows</i> which projects over the eyes
			and is knitted in frowning (<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				780b28
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶν δέ τ᾽ ἐπισκύνιον</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτω ἕλκεται ὄσσε καλύπτων</span>, of
			a lion, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.136
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεινὸν ἐ. ξυνάγων</span>, of
			Aeschylus, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				823
			</span></i> (hex.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖον ἐ. βλοσυρῷ ἐπέκειτο προσώπῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					24.118
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.100
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυσὸν ἐ., πολιὸν ἐ.</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.64
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Sil.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				7.117
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Zenod.
			</span></i>); even <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαιδρὸν ἐ</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.159
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστρέψας γυρὸν</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>., of one who puts on a wise face,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				11.376.8
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.414e
			</span></i>: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>.
				<i>superciliousness</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυμνώσαντο</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίου παντὸς ἐ</span>., of Diogenes, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.63
			</span></i>, etc.; but in <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				25.3.6
			</span></i>, simply, <i>austerity, gravity of deportment.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>. Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκύνιος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <i>supercilious,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
